<table>
<tr><th>Expression</th><th>Result</th></tr>
<tr><td>x[0][1][2]</td><td>60</td></tr>
<tr><td>x[1][0][1]</td><td>80 (not 70 — 70 is [1][0][0])</td></tr>
<tr><td>x[2][0][0]</td><td>RE `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` — top level has no index 2</td></tr>
<tr><td>x[1][2][0]</td><td>RE `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` — x[1] has no index 2</td></tr>
<tr><td>x[1][1][1]</td><td>100</td></tr>
<tr><td>x[2][1][0] (he also rattles extra indexes like x[2][2][1][0])</td><td>AIOOB — index 2 does not exist at the top</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Code</th><th>Valid?</th><th>Result</th></tr>
<tr><td>s.length</td><td>yes</td><td>3 — s is an array; three elements</td></tr>
<tr><td>s.length()</td><td>no</td><td>CE cannot find symbol: method length, location class `String[]` (caption “Stringer” = String array type)</td></tr>
<tr><td>s[0].length</td><td>no</td><td>CE cannot find symbol: variable length, location class `java.lang.String`</td></tr>
<tr><td>s[0].length()</td><td>yes</td><td>1 — first element is &quot;A&quot;</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Array type</th><th>Allowed element types</th></tr>
<tr><td>Primitive arrays</td><td>any type which can be implicitly promoted to the declared type</td></tr>
<tr><td>Object type arrays</td><td>declared type or its child-class objects</td></tr>
<tr><td>Abstract class type arrays</td><td>child-class objects</td></tr>
<tr><td>Interface type arrays</td><td>implementation-class objects</td></tr>
</table>
